# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# sim_versions.env — pinned upstream simulator versions (SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH).
#
# sim/metalab/setup.sh clones each engine's upstream repo to a SIBLING of this repo and checks out
# EXACTLY the commit pinned here; learning/scripts/local/setup_env.sh reads the same pins, so the
# `rl_train.sh` auto-restore path uses them too. These refs MUST match the commit the shared S3
# conda-env snapshot was built against (see "Updating a sim version" in sim/metalab/README.md).
#
# Bumping a version (env owner only, on a VALIDATED update):
#   1) set the *_REF below to the new commit
#   2) re-checkout the sibling + re-lock: `sim/metalab/setup.sh` (or `uv lock` in sim/metalab/<engine>)
#   3) commit sim_versions.env + the updated uv.lock, merge — teammates re-run sim/metalab/setup.sh to converge
#
# Clone URLs are overridable from the env (e.g. a fork); the refs here are authoritative.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

: "${NEWTON_GIT:=https://github.com/newton-physics/newton.git}"
# v1.5.0 (2026-08-11, "Prepare Newton 1.5.0 release" #3884) — the newest upstream release; main carries
# 281 more commits but no tag. Previous pin was v1.4.0 (0597c719, 2026-07-16).
# THE ENGINE BUMP IS NOT SEPARABLE from its deps: v1.5.0 declares warp-lang>=1.16.0 and
# mujoco-warp~=3.11.0, and newton carries NO import-time version guard, so a source-only upgrade fails at
# the FIRST KERNEL COMPILE, not at import — measured: `wp.quat_twist_angle_signed` missing under the older
# warp, raised from sim/articulation.py while building eval_articulation_ik. Any A/B against v1.4.0
# therefore measures newton + mujoco-warp + warp together, never one of them.
# What it does NOT fix (verified byte-identical across the two tags): shape_collision_aabb_lower/upper is
# still baked at finalize and still absent from ModelFlags.SHAPE_PROPERTIES, so the per-env rewrite in
# backends/newton/backend.py:set_object_scale stays load-bearing; per-world geom_dataid is still
# template-only, so mjw_object_scale.py cannot go either.
NEWTON_REF="cca3bb8a17a3620a1343df3cf12c625e4161b317"

: "${GENESIS_WORLD_GIT:=https://github.com/Genesis-Embodied-AI/genesis-world.git}"
GENESIS_WORLD_REF="491d41e2e8dd7527be00c154198857d6aaefb793"
